'' RUN: 'sizeof( (int32, string) )' and 'len( (int32, string) )' name a TUPLE TYPE. With a type
'' keyword, PTR or 'name as T' inside, the operand went to the expression parser, came out
'' untyped, and the build stopped at TKO0994. Each size here matches the typedef'd type's,
'' and the expression operands that also hold a type keyword stay expressions.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/sizeof-tuple-type.bas -o tests/codegen/sizeoftupletype.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/codegen/sizeoftupletype.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 32 32 32
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 32 32
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 32 24
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 32 8 32
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 3 16
